					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13875580</guid>
				<title>SCP-5083</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13875580/scp-5083</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2020 00:44:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>7ballcraze</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3426641</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>alright here's why</p> <blockquote> <p>Scp 5083 - The Reality Remote</p> </blockquote> <p>The title already made me do -1. It's formatted wrong. SCP is suppose to be uppercase and The Reality Remote part shouldn't be there.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Item #: SCP-5083</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Uhhh only the parts before the : gets bolded. This applies to every single one.</p> <blockquote> <p>SCP-5083 is to be kept in a wooden box measuring 5.5 inches in width and 3.5 inches in length.</p> </blockquote> <p>This is a common problem with newer SCP writers, they put everything in boxes. You can just say SCP-XXXX is put in a locker. Not everything needs it's own room. Also the site uses meters not inches.</p> <blockquote> <p>Due to SCP-5083 being used for personal gain becoming a possibility, SCP-5083's box is to be under 24/7 surveillance.</p> </blockquote> <p>Reading on the effects of the SCP, I don't really understand this. If it was a box that gave you 1 million dollars but also blew up a small town then yeah sure but all this SCP does is change reality. Also I'm pretty sure everything is under constant surveillance.</p> <blockquote> <p>Any individual attempting to interact in any way with SCP-5083 without authorization from the 05-Council is to be immediately terminated.</p> </blockquote> <p>Uh, what. I'm like 95% sure that termination would be kind of strict. Unless this can cause an end of the world scenario then probably not have the termination. Also it's O5 not 05.</p> <blockquote> <p>SCP-5083 is a standard black universal tv remote measuring 2 inches in width and 7.5 inches in length.</p> </blockquote> <p>You don't have to say every since detail unless it's anomalous. For example: I don't have to say &quot;SCP-XXXX is a computer that has a screen the size of 0.4318 meters.&quot; Like that's kind of silly. It would be acceptable if it was something like &quot;SCP-XXXX is an Asian Child measuring 492 feet in height&quot;.</p> <blockquote> <p>Each button on SCP-5038 seemingly has a different effect on reality but can be made to effect one specific item or individual by pointing SCP-5083 at the target and pressing a button.</p> </blockquote> <p>And that's the end&#8230; It would have really been spiced up with some test logs. I wanna see what scientists can do with this remote. Like what <strong>can</strong> you do with it</p> <p>Overall, go to the forums. This is probably a cold post.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
